  "CHOLESTEROL":                               { role: "Barrière", description: "It's one of the important lipids that can be found naturally in the outer layer of the skin. About25% of the goopy stuff between our skin cells consists of cholesterol. Together withceramidesand fatty acids, they play avital role in having a healthy skin barrierand keeping the..." },
  "GLYCERIN":                                  { role: "Barrière", description: "Glycerin doesn’t sound very glamorous but it is a realoldie but a goodie. It’s been used in cosmetics for more than 50 years and it’s a totally natural ingredient that’s also in the outermost layer of our skin (called stratum corneum - SC)." },
  "GLYCEROL":                                  { role: "Barrière", description: "Glycerin doesn’t sound very glamorous but it is a realoldie but a goodie. It’s been used in cosmetics for more than 50 years and it’s a totally natural ingredient that’s also in the outermost layer of our skin (called stratum corneum - SC)." },
